Subject: [PATCH 2/5] [M156] [Extensions] Validate pending script input in
 ScriptInjectionTracker

Original change's description:
> [Extensions] Validate pending script input in ScriptInjectionTracker
>
> Previously, ScriptInjectionTracker::WillExecuteCode() for
> ExtensionActionRunner unconditionally recorded a content script
> execution for the target renderer process when handling
> RequestScriptInjectionPermission() or running pending scripts. It did
> not verify whether the browser had actually dispatched a withheld
> programmatic or declarative JavaScript injection to that frame, or
> whether the extension had matching content scripts.
>
> Update ScriptExecutor and RequestContentScript to record withheld
> JavaScript injections as pending in ScriptInjectionTracker when
> dispatched. ScriptInjectionTracker now validates this pending state
> before marking the renderer process as having executed a content or user
> script from the extension.
>
